	<div class="content-box">
		<p class="center-text text-medium">If Agent Whirlwind Ever Found Out</h3>
		<p class="center-text">The transcript of an audio log that Agent Whirlwind would leave behind if she were to ever discover that she is half-angel, and that Urbanshade had been keeping it a secret to her in order to maximize her 'efficiency'</p>
	</div>

	<div>
		<p class="center-text text-medium">I know how the system works, anyone with the right clearance can listen to this.</p>
		<p class="center-text text-medium">And don't even bother trying to drug me up with amnestics; we're all well aware that it won't do shit.</p>
		<p class="center-text text-medium">To anyone who isn't Mr.Shade, know that I hold no negativity to you, you are just trying to be the light in a sea of darkness.</p>
		<p class="center-text text-medium">So, I end off with one final message to you, Mr.Shade.</p>
		<p class="center-text text-medium">I knew monsters were real the day your organization recruited me—the day the cuts I made on my arms would finally mend.</p>
		<p class="center-text text-medium">You taught me that as a kid, the monster under my bed wasn't my imagination, but I could have never fathomed that I would be working for one.</p>
		<p class="center-text text-medium">And you of all people should know the weight behind these words, knowing this comes from the gal who looked her parents' murderer in the eye and offered forgiveness:</p>
		<p class="center-text text-medium">when your stupid immortality crystal finally runs out, and you spend your last fleeting moments withering away in that wheelchair, may you rot in hell, you tank-treading bastard.</p>
